# Change: Am-E and E-B7 (repertoire plan: st-change-am-e-e-b7). An original chord-change study.
# Each half is a ladder that changes faster and faster: the home chord held for two bars (one
# strum a bar), then a change every bar with two strums, every bar with four strums, and every
# two beats. First half (home Am, the i and V of A minor): Am (x02210) with E (022100), the same
# shape moved one string toward string 6. Second half (home E, the I and V7 of E major): E with
# B7 (x21202); finger 2 stays on string 5, fret 2 (B). Strum Am and B7 on strings 5 to 1, E on
# all six. Keep the metronome on: the new chord lands on the beat even if the strum before it
# catches open strings. The last E is held for two beats to close.
# The teacher plays an original tune over your chords, a chord tone on every strong beat; each
# half closes with its leading note rising to the home note (G# to A, then D# to E).
title: Change: Am-E and E-B7
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original chord-change study
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 3
tags: chord changes, strumming, metronome, anchor finger
tempo: 72
time: 4/4
key: Am

track: Your strum
